{"id": "EUVD-2026-81851", "enisaUuid": "636d3fa0-0b93-3006-b907-20725b309430", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: airoha: add missed IRQ resource helpers\n\nWithout hooking .irq_request_resources, gpiolib cannot set\nGPIOD_FLAG_USED_AS_IRQ. This breaks pin direction locking and can allow\nuserspace or another driver to reconfigure an active IRQ pin as an output", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fda7350f257e59eee1bc7537c202e36bd56aea97", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c968c11592b478af4fbcb9453a0e1ac664c2e90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a02fa031b9520e46e98bff17e12b472eba770670"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90258", "GHSA-cg6w-564g-phrg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "178810eb-4201-3e91-9cbb-fdf8da81307f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1c8ace2d0725c1c8d5012f8a56c5fb31805aad27 <fda7350f257e59eee1bc7537c202e36bd56aea97"}, {"id": "694c14f9-9daf-3571-be1a-db4a920afd58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "76f9d51a-a720-36c3-a806-a6b2f2efbfb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1c8ace2d0725c1c8d5012f8a56c5fb31805aad27 <2c968c11592b478af4fbcb9453a0e1ac664c2e90"}, {"id": "7e9b13a5-2a3c-38fc-8399-53c40fa36574", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1c8ace2d0725c1c8d5012f8a56c5fb31805aad27 <a02fa031b9520e46e98bff17e12b472eba770670"}, {"id": "8d009384-f9c1-3b9a-9313-75cbfb816b7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "8f07a821-14b3-37f9-be23-f1a1c07ca694", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "9d31a52a-bfcb-3b47-8bbc-f0ca9f38424b", "product": {"name": "Lin